WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:18.150 align:start position:0%
 
you feel  Resident Evil 7 is Capcom's attempt to  make its beloved horror franchise scary  again by taking the series original  formula of claustrophobic locations and  limited ammo and mixing it with newer  horror concepts like first-person  cat-and-mouse chases this first-person  perspective also allows for a new way to  play virtual reality just an altered  Resident Evil 7 is a big deal for VR  because unlike Batman Arkham VR or  whatever that Final Fantasy 15 thing is  this isn't a short experience re 7 is a  big-budget triple-a numbered sequence so  I saw a golden opportunity by playing  the entirety of Resident Evil 7 in psvr  the whole thing which means experiencing  moments like this and this  and this  [Music]  the game does a good job offering  several adjustable options in VR like  field-of-view  walking speed and Crouch the big thing  is camera rotation options but I'll  admit that none of them are perfect on  the default setting the camera snaps at  angles of 30 45 and 90 degrees this is  the safest option if you want to  minimize the risk of motion sickness but  the jerky nature of it took me out of  the experience the option I used is  called smoothing and while I felt a  little sick at first I was able to get  used to it and play the whole game this  way I would seriously advise caution  though when trying this setting and if  you're prone to motion sickness I would  avoid it all together issues like this  are partly due to the fact that Resident  Evil 7 isn't designed to be VR only it  has to work as a traditional game - this  means no use of PlayStation Move  controllers to simulate your hands the  most you get is the camera is now  controlled by your head so Resident  Evil's virtual reality is less about  enhancing the gameplay experience and  more about immersing you in its  environment the true strength of playing  something in VR is the sense of presence  you gain you are more aware of what's  around you and what's behind you you can  tell how long a hallway is and how close  an enemy is with greater accuracy  you really feel like you are walking  around this mansion and Resident Evil  seven is the perfect game for this  because its environmental design and art  are top-notch the realistic art style  fits perfectly every room is full of  notes to read pictures to look at and  the disgusting imagery my god it's  almost too gross to look at sometimes  this game is gnarly and fantastically  disgusting  regardless of how you play it but being  able to see it so up close without that  disconnect between you and the TV really  makes your stomach churn now let's talk  about everyone's favorite part the  scares there are plenty of those in your  face jump scares that will get you for  sure but for me the memorable moments  come from entering a new location for  the first time and just having to walk  through it you have no idea what's going  to happen next and that is just the  worst feeling I hated and I mean hated  the old house it's dark it's rotting and  I seriously wanted to take the headset  off when the giant bugs showed up we'd  be here all day if I mentioned every  memorable moment but a few standout  scares include crawling inside this wall  full of centipedes walking through neck  eye water and the entirety of this  location after beating the game I went  back in played outside of the AR to see  if there are any differences and the  answer is yes for one it's way easier in  my opinion to shoot in VR because you  can aim with your head this might make  the game slightly easier in VR but I  never found the difficulty balance to be  an issue when playing  this also means if you freak out or try  and look away it messes up your shot  which is pretty neat side note it is  possible to use your added camera  movement from VR to slightly break the  illusion of some scenes it doesn't ruin  anything but it's pretty funny another  thing is that a lot of character  animations are absent in VR stuff like  getting knocked down or jumped by an  enemy doesn't happen this is most likely  because taking camera control away from  you for even a moment would induce  motion sickness having played in VR  first I never missed these animations or  notice their absence but playing it  again I was surprised how many of them  were taken out of course sometimes the  game can't cut scripted moments when  they are story related so to avoid  motion sickness again jarring Lea  switches you to floating in a black void  with a screen playing a pre-rendered  cutscenes in front of you it's the worst  part of the VR experience and that it  quickly reminds you that you are playing  a video game perhaps the strangest part  of playing Resident Evil 7 a second time  without VR is that I think playing in VR  first actually kind of ruined the game  for me it's like when you go back and  we'll get vacation photos it's the same  thing but everything is flat now you  aren't there in the same way there's a  real lack of punch to it don't get me  wrong I still think Resident Evil 7 is a  great game but this is a weird and  slightly amusing issue that I think a  lot of people who play this in VR first  will experience you might also be  wondering what it's like to play a nine  hour game from start to finish in VR  well I wouldn't recommend playing it all  in one day like I did because at the end  of the night my eyes felt really awful  after having a screen stuck to them all  day but other than that I felt fine  you think I'd have wanted to take a  break to save my heart from all the  tension and scares but honestly I was  enjoying the game so much I just kept  wanting to play it  [Music]  my first playthrough of Resident Evil 7  is gonna stick with me as one of those  memorable gaming experiences partly due  to playing it in VR even if it's not a  perfect example of how the technology  can reshape games as we know them  getting to see the Baker Mansion for the  first time that way is something you  only get one chance at and if you have  the opportunity to experience it this  way I highly recommend it it's good by  the way if you are interested in just  watching a bunch of people get scared  playing Resident Evil 7 NVR there is a  video where I threw a bunch of games on  ploy ease into a room for your enjoyment  yeah oh you and if you have played resin  evil 7 in VR or if you want to try it  now let me know in the comments  [Music]

